  "body": "Part of #2238 (frame cost: calculate before and cache). Measured with the frame-cost probe of #2238, release build, fig8.step.\n\n## What happens\n\n`interact::selection_feature_lines` (`crates/ui/src/interact.rs`) makes the overlay lines of the shown picks on each scene collection. It reads the operation from the world and calls `feature_lines` for each pick each time.\n\n| State | Piece | ms per frame (release) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2D Adaptive on one welded face | `scene/overlay.selection_features` | 1.48 |\n| 2D Adaptive on one welded face | `ui/viewport.pick_ink` | 0.96 |\n\n## Done means\n\n- The overlay lines are made when the shown picks or the model change, and read from a cache on other frames. The cache is in a `ui` module next to `selection_feature_lines` (for example `frame_memo`), not in a widget.\n- The key follows `docs/decisions/2238-frame-cost-rule.md`: the pick list value and the `Arc` of the model features.\n- A counter test: a still frame makes zero new line sets.\n- A changed-input test: a new pick gives new lines, equal to a fresh calculation.\n- The probe `frame_cost_probe` shows the piece under 0.1 ms in release.\n",
